BIG spoilers ahead...



























                   SOME COMMON INSTANT DEATHS
                     and how to avoid them


1.  Petrified by Medusa
Solution:  If you enter a level with lots of water, put on a blindfold
(you should have telepathy by now) and check for Medusa.  Don't enter
her room unless you're blind.  Also, if you're around medusa's level
(in the 20's), and you fall through a trapdoor, put blindfolds on
before going up stairs.

2.  Hit by a death ray/black dragon breath.
Solution:  Shield of reflection/amulet of reflection.  SoR is always
my first wish.

3.  Drowned by an eel.
Solution:  Unless you have an amulet of magical breathing, stay away
from ;s.  Levitation/water walking will not protect you.

4.  Cockatrices
Solution:  Keep lizard corpses on handy if you get into hand-to-hand
conflict.  If necessary, pray.  Don't pick up their corpses with bare
hands.  Don't wander around places where they may have died while
blind.  If you do elect to carry them, be aware that trapdoors, pits,
and (if you're burdened) staircases spell death.

5.  Praying in Gehennom
Solution:  Don't do it.

6.  Choked on a corpse
Solution:  Amulets of Magical Breathing will save you.  If the game
asks "Stop eating?" the answer is "yes."  You won't always be warned,
so realize that eating when satiated is risky.

7.  Digested
Solution:  Trappers and Purple Worms are bad news.  If one swallows
you, get out FAST.  Wands of digging are useful.

8.  Juiblex
Solution:  Wand of digging will get you out of Juiblex.  Unicorn horns
will make you your usual chipper self again.

9.  Crushed by a bit of flying metal
Solution:  Destroy the drawbridge yourself, from a fair distance.
Find some other way into the castle.  Hopefully (IMHO) this will be
changed in the next version.

10.  The other three horsemen of the Apocalypse.
Solution:  Only Death is instantly fatal.  Generally, though, avoid &s
on the astral plane.

Anyone think of any others?

